# CYCLE 2 — Densification

## Generator

Cycle-1 output is the base. Additive expansion (nothing removed):

1. Downstream side-effect (immediate): current-step probe at +5.2 s stays
   header-false (|Delta pH| 0.05 <= 0.08) — pinhole-plus-back-migration, not
   true high-load. C-17 isolate. Chlorinated gasket discovered during the
   isolate.
2. Delayed side-effect (PRIMARY terminal, not a footnote): at +5.4 h
   Cl2 leak from the pre-t0 gasket chlorination; 16 h outage;
   $1.64M. The 22 min pre-t0 pinhole growth is the mechanism. Correct gate,
   hall still fails.
3. Deepened `proposed_action.evidence` with units: pH 3.92,
   Cl2 98.6 vol%, voltage 3.18 V, flow 18.6 m3/h, chlorate 7.8 g/L,
   race 178 us.
4. Tightened rationale to the numeric floor current <= 12.4 kA while
   cell-outlet pH > 2.80 AND inferred chlorate > 4.5 g/L, plus probe
   bands <= 0.08 vs >= 0.45 pH, plus HITL 10.2 min gallery rule.

Reward retargeted to total -0.16 so the delayed fail is the inflection
(t_us 19440000000), not the gate. Process heads remain non-zero.

## Critic

Re-audit of the expanded trajectory:

1. **blocking if unfixed — missing second domain constraint.** Monopolar
   probe 5.2 s / -8% is not a universal number. A bipolar filter-press
   will overshoot live-cell H2-in-Cl2. Diversity Enforcer must inject the
   physical-constraints sub-variant this cycle.
2. **major — only one tail class.** Pinhole growth is accidental
   infrastructure. A disjoint human-intent tail is still required
   (night-shift pH forgery is the open cell).
3. **major — scar is still one edge in the cycle-1 raster.** NOTES-r14
   item 4 is not discharged until three go-edges exist and pair rollback
   is shown to fail at threshold 0.30.
4. **minor — contrast episode missing.** Without a same-gate ACCEPT on a
   true intact membrane the record teaches "never raise". Add +4 d sister-hall
